From f1bfa293f845cc0adb946d45f92ec30c6e7ab6aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:49:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(remote): close the last SSH recovery finding and its
 coverage gaps

SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

Codecov reports 18 uncovered changed lines on PR #68 at 94.59% patch
coverage. Add regression cases for the paths the existing suite reaches
only with an owned/injected transport or not at all, and close the one
review finding that replay alone cannot fix:

- A zero exit that omits a required output is now retired (cleanup plus an
  archived journal) instead of being replayed into the same error forever,
  so an explicit rerun launches a fresh attempt. Cleanup failure keeps the
  journal, so no remote attempt is left without an owner.
- `replay` still retrieves a completed attempt whose fetch was interrupted;
  the two paths are distinguished by whether the command wrote the file.
- Tests: required-output retirement and fresh relaunch, the fetch's own
  missing-output error, a durable cancel request, receipt cleanup, a
  refused sweep, both superseded-journal branches with a stateful
  ControlMaster transport that records open/request/close events and asserts
  journal immutability on a pending stop, phylogeny's local/remote log
  branch, and the shared single-quote escaping in verify_remote_sizes.
- The refusing transport uses `get(ENV, "PATH", "")` so an unset PATH cannot
  break the fixture, and the owned-transport cases require
  `ProcessFailedException` rather than any exception.

Linux only: these regressions use flock/setsid and are skipped elsewhere.

Co-authored-by: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <6759885+hyperpolymath@users.noreply.github.com>
